---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import TimeSeriesChart from "../components/TimeSeriesChart.astro";
import execution from "../../public/data/execution_latest.json";

function fmt(n, d = 3) { return (n === null || n === undefined || Number.isNaN(n)) ? "n/a" : n.toFixed(d); }
function signed(n, d = 2) { return (n === null || n === undefined || Number.isNaN(n)) ? "n/a" : (n >= 0 ? "+" : "") + n.toFixed(d); }
---
<Base title="Execution Edge Monitor" description="Weekly bot-retail Prelec alpha gap from 233M Polymarket trades.">
  <h1>Execution Edge Monitor</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">The bot-minus-retail Prelec alpha gap. A behavioral proxy for execution-quality divergence.</p>

  <p>
    As of <strong>{execution.as_of}</strong>, the alpha gap stands at <strong>{signed(execution.value, 3)}</strong>,
    with a 52-week rolling z-score of <strong>{signed(execution.z52w, 2)}</strong>.
    Bot Prelec alpha: <strong>{fmt(execution.per_type_alpha.bot?.alpha, 3)}</strong>.
    Active retail Prelec alpha: <strong>{fmt(execution.per_type_alpha.active_retail?.alpha, 3)}</strong>.
    Week based on <strong>{execution.n_trades_week?.toLocaleString?.() ?? execution.n_trades_week}</strong> trades across all classes.
  </p>

  <h2>Weekly history</h2>
  <TimeSeriesChart
    dataUrl="/data/execution_timeseries.json"
    yField="alpha_gap"
    smoothField="alpha_gap_ma13w"
    yLabel="bot alpha minus retail alpha"
    zeroLine={true}
  />
  <p class="muted" style="font-size:14px; margin-top:-18px;">
    A positive gap indicates bots weight tails more heavily than active retail. The bold line is a 13-week moving average.
  </p>

  <h2>Current per-type alphas</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Wallet class</th><th>Prelec alpha</th></tr>
    {Object.entries(execution.per_type_alpha).map(([k, v]) => (
      <tr><td>{k}</td><td class="mono">{fmt((v as any).alpha, 3)}</td></tr>
    ))}
  </table>

  <h2>52-week rolling statistics on the gap</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Statistic</th><th>Value</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Mean</td><td class="mono">{fmt(execution.rolling.mean_52w, 3)}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SD</td><td class="mono">{fmt(execution.rolling.sd_52w, 3)}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Min</td><td class="mono">{fmt(execution.rolling.min_52w, 3)}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Max</td><td class="mono">{fmt(execution.rolling.max_52w, 3)}</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Methodology</h2>
  <p>
    For each wallet class (bot, active retail, sophisticated, casual, one-shot), we fit a one-parameter Prelec
    weighting function to that class's weekly calibration curve. The resulting alpha captures how strongly the
    class distorts probabilities away from the identity. The Execution Edge gap is alpha(bot) - alpha(active
    retail). In Paper 1, bots capture -4.25 bps effective spread on their trades while active retail pays +11.68
    bps; the alpha gap is the behavioral signature of that divergence and tracks it week-by-week.
  </p>

  <h2>Data</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/data/execution_history.csv">execution_history.csv</a>
    {' '}(wide, {execution.n_weeks_history} weeks from {execution.first_date})
    &middot;
    <a href="/data/execution_by_type_history.csv">execution_by_type_history.csv</a> (long)
    &middot;
    <a href="/data/execution_latest.json">execution_latest.json</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Cite</h2>
  <div class="citation">{`@misc{dellavedova2026execution,
  title        = {Execution Edge Monitor},
  author       = {Della Vedova, Joshua},
  year         = {2026},
  version      = {0.1.0},
  publisher    = {University of San Diego},
  url          = {https://jdellavedova.com/execution}
}`}</div>
</Base>
